(FMT-24: the ASSIGNMENT half of "Format Strings as Values" —
 LANGUAGE.md:3424-3427 says a format string works as a text initializer
 AND an assignment; every existing leaf only ever exercises the
 initializer ('gen leaf format value's 'token decl'/'path decl') — grep
 for `Set <text> to "{` across every src/gen_*.vox file finds nothing
 before this. Verified, not merely emitted: the second `Set` reads the
 counter's value AFTER it changed, so the assertion would catch a
 compiler that quietly kept the format string's ORIGINAL value on
 reassignment. Hand-verified against vox 0.4.14 and the 0.4.15 stack —
 docs/ledger/probes/input-output/FMT-24.vox, REPORT-LEAVES-FMT-A.md.)

