(FMT-29: LANGUAGE.md:3441-3442 — each format-string evaluation
 allocates a NEW string, so the source buffer can be cleared and
 refilled without disturbing a text already made from it. No existing
 leaf clears a USER buffer after making a text from it before this (grep-
 confirmed: `clear` on a user buffer appears in no leaf; buffers.md's own
 BUF-33 records the same absence for the generator's own accumulator,
 `gen_out`). Two texts made from the SAME buffer, one before and one
 after a clear-and-refill, each asserted against its own generation-
 time-known content — if the first text were secretly aliased to the
 buffer instead of an independent copy, the refill would corrupt it and
 the first assertion would catch it. Hand-verified against vox 0.4.14
 and the 0.4.15 stack — docs/ledger/probes/input-output/FMT-29.vox,
 REPORT-LEAVES-FMT-A.md.)

