(FMT-41: the "or file handle" half of Declarations in Branches —
 LANGUAGE.md:3460-3464. The manual's own worked example (3466-3474) opens
 the SAME handle name on both arms of an if/otherwise and writes to it
 afterward, and never closes it; this leaf emits that shape with the
 target varying instead of the manual's flag-conditioned path, so the
 branch that runs varies with the draw instead of always being the same
 one. No assertion: there is nothing to read back (a generated program
 cannot read its own stdout), so this leaf's proof is that the program
 COMPILES and runs to exit 0 — if the "every branch" scoping ever
 regressed for a file handle, that would surface as a parser-reject
 finding, not silence.

 The `If` arm opens at fd 1; the `Otherwise` arm opens a path inside the
 program's own confined scratch directory (the same `gen_scratch_flag`/
 `gen_does_file_io` machinery every file leaf in gen_files.vox uses,
 including its Defect-16 guard — stand aside via `gen leaf print` when
 the binding isn't there rather than build a path from an empty flag).
 NOT fd 2: an earlier version of this leaf opened the `Otherwise` arm at
 fd 2 (stderr), which is the harness's own channel, not the generated
 program's — `tests/270_layout` folds a run's stderr into its captured
 output, so every one of its 64 programs that happened to draw this leaf
 and take the `Otherwise` branch failed that test's golden diff. Master
 review round 3 caught it; fixed by moving the second target off any
 standard stream entirely, onto the same sandboxed-path pattern the FILES
 surface already established.

 Deliberately NEVER `Close`s the handle, matching the manual's own
 example: hand-reduced during this batch's own campaign that `Close` on
 a handle opened at a numeric fd (`at 1`, also confirmed at `at 2`)
 closes the real underlying descriptor, not an independent copy — every
 `Print` for the rest of that PROCESS then goes nowhere, silently, exit
 0. Three of this batch's own campaign findings were an unrelated leaf's
 assertion firing correctly but its message vanishing into this hole.
 Recorded as a candidate in REPORT-LEAVES-FMT-A.md, not adjudicated here
 — this leaf works around it by simply never closing what it opens,
 the same restraint the manual's own worked example already shows.

 FMT-40 (the plain-VARIABLE half of this same claim) and FMT-42
 (functions reading such a variable) are deliberately NOT here:
 hand-verification found the plain-variable case does not compile
 ('outcome' is used before it is declared, on both compilers) even
 though this file-handle case does. Recorded as a candidate in
 REPORT-LEAVES-FMT-A.md, not adjudicated here — those two rows stay
 `todo`, blocked on that finding.

 Hand-verified against vox 0.4.14 and the 0.4.15 stack —
 docs/ledger/probes/input-output/FMT-41.vox already covers the manual's
 own shape; REPORT-LEAVES-FMT-A.md has this leaf's own repro.)

