(FMT-52, FMT-54: LANGUAGE.md:3499-3506's own chain shape — clauses after
 the first carry NO leading comma, and the chain may continue with
 `and if` as well as `but if`. `gen leaf butif print` (gen_flow.vox, out
 of this surface's own scope to edit) puts a comma before EVERY clause
 and never emits `and if` at all — grep-confirmed zero `and if`
 occurrences across all eight src/gen_*.vox files before this leaf.

 No assertion: like FMT-51/53/55 already exercised elsewhere, WHICH
 clause of a conditional print fired is only observable in Print's own
 stdout, and a generated program has no way to read that back (the same
 limit that leaves FMT-04/05/06 exercised only — see the report). Three
 clauses, an operand and two bounds all drawn per program, so first-
 match-wins and default-fallthrough both vary which line the campaign
 sees, even though nothing here asserts which one it was.

 Hand-verified against vox 0.4.14 and the 0.4.15 stack that the comma-
 less/and-if chain compiles and that first-match-wins and default-
 fallthrough both still hold, by eye — docs/ledger/probes/input-output/
 FMT-52.vox and FMT-54.vox already cover the underlying grammar;
 REPORT-LEAVES-FMT-A.md has this leaf's own repro.)

